# Auth & Data Isolation with Clerk

All auth is handled by Clerk. Users must only ever be able to read or mutate their own data.

## Getting the current user

In Server Components and Route Handlers, always resolve the user with `auth()` from `@clerk/nextjs/server` and reject unauthenticated requests immediately.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — server component or route handler
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";

const { userId } = await auth();
if (!userId) {
  // In a Route Handler:
  return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });
  // In a Server Component: redirect("/sign-in") or notFound()
}
```

## Scoping Drizzle queries to the current user

Always filter by `userId` on every read and write. Never fetch a resource by `id` alone — always include the ownership check in the same query.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — fetches any deck regardless of owner
const deck = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(eq(decksTable.id, deckId));

// ✅ GOOD — ownership enforced at the DB layer
const deck = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));
```

The same pattern applies to mutations:

```typescript
// ✅ UPDATE — scope to owner
await db
  .update(decksTable)
  .set({ title })
  .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));

// ✅ DELETE — scope to owner
await db
  .delete(decksTable)
  .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));
```

## Cards (owned via deck)

`cardsTable` has no direct `userId`. Join through `decksTable` to verify ownership:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — verify the parent deck belongs to the user
const [card] = await db
  .select({ card: cardsTable })
  .from(cardsTable)
  .innerJoin(decksTable, eq(cardsTable.deckId, decksTable.id))
  .where(and(eq(cardsTable.id, cardId), eq(decksTable.userId, userId)));

if (!card) return new Response("Not Found", { status: 404 });
```

## Return 404, not 403, for unauthorized resource access

When a user requests a resource that exists but belongs to someone else, respond with `404 Not Found`. This avoids leaking the existence of other users' data.
